{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-jer-18-1","title":"Jeremiah 18:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Under the type of a potter is shewn God's absolute power in disposing of nations. 11 Judgments threatened to Judah for her strange revolt. 18 Jeremiah prays against his conspirators.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-2","title":"Jeremiah 18:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>A.M. 3396. B.C. 608. and go. 13:1; 19:1,2; Isa 20:2; Eze 4:1-5:1; Am 7:7; Heb 1:1 cause. 23:22; Ac 9:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-3","title":"Jeremiah 18:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>I went. Jon 1:3; Joh 15:14; Ac 26:19 wheels. or, frames, or seats.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-4","title":"Jeremiah 18:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>made of clay was marred in. or, made was marred, as clay in.made it again. Heb. returned and made. as. 6; Isa 45:9; Ro 9:20-23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-6","title":"Jeremiah 18:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>4; Isa 64:8; Da 4:23; Mt 20:15; Ro 11:34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-7","title":"Jeremiah 18:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>to pluck. 1:10; 12:14-17; 25:9-14; 45:4; Am 9:8; Jon 3:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-8","title":"Jeremiah 18:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>that nation. 7:3-7; 36:3; Jud 10:15,16; 1Ki 8:33,34; 2Ch 12:6; Isa 1:16-19 Eze 18:21; 33:11,13; Jon 2:5-10; Lu 13:3-5 I will. 15:6; 26:3,13; 42:10; Ex 32:12; De 32:36; Jud 2:18; Ps 90:13 Ps 106:45; 135:14; Ho 11:8; Joe 2:13,14; Am 7:3-6; Jon 3:9,10; 4:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-9","title":"Jeremiah 18:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>to build. 1:10; 11:17; 30:18; 31:4,28,38; 32:41; Ec 3:2; Am 9:11-15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-10","title":"Jeremiah 18:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>do. 7:23-28; Ps 125:5; Eze 18:24; 33:18; 45:20; Zep 1:6 then. Nu 14:22,34; 1Sa 2:30; 13:13; 15:11,35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-11","title":"Jeremiah 18:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>go to. Ge 11:3,4,7; 2Ki 5:5; Isa 5:5; Jas 4:13; 5:1 and devise. 18; 4:23; 11:19; 51:11; Mic 2:3 return. 3:1,22; 7:3; 25:5; 26:3,13; 35:15; 36:3,7; 2Ki 17:13; 22:13 Isa 1:16-19; 55:6,7; La 3:39-41; Eze 13:22; 18:23,30-32; Zec 1:3 Ac 26:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-12","title":"Jeremiah 18:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>There. 2:25; 2Ki 6:33; Isa 57:10; Eze 37:11 we will walk. 3:17; 7:24; 11:8; 16:12; 23:17; 44:17; Ge 6:5; 8:21; De 29:19 Mr 7:21,22; Lu 1:51</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-13","title":"Jeremiah 18:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Ask. 2:10-13 who. 1Sa 4:7; Isa 66:8; 1Co 5:1 virgin. 2:13; 14:17; 31:4; Isa 36:22; La 1:15 a very. 5:30; 23:14; Ho 6:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-14","title":"Jeremiah 18:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>Will. Joh 6:68 the snow, etc. or, my fields for a rock, or for the snow ofLebanon? shall the running waters be forsaken for the strange cold waters? Parkhurst renders, \"Will the snow of Lebanon fail from the rock of the field? or will the issuing cold flowing waters (from that mountain namely) be exhausted?\" (See Targ., LXX., and Vulg.) No more could I fail my people if they trusted in me. (Compare ch. 2:13.) Maundrell says, \"The chief benefit the mountain of Lebanon serves for, is, that by its exceeding height, it proves a conservatory for abundance of snow, which thawing in the heat of summer, affords supplies of water to the rivers and fountains in the valleys below.\"</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-15","title":"Jeremiah 18:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>my people. 2:13,19,32; 3:21; 13:25; 17:13 burned. 10:15; 16:19; 44:15-19,25; Isa 41:29; 65:7; Ho 2:13; 11:2 caused. Isa 3:12; 9:16; Mal 2:8; Mt 15:6; Ro 14:21 the ancient. 6:16 to walk. 19:5; Isa 57:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-16","title":"Jeremiah 18:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>make. 9:11; 19:8; 25:9; 49:13; 50:13; Le 26:33,34,43; De 29:23; Isa 6:11 Eze 6:14; 12:19; 33:28,29 a perpetual. 1Ki 9:8; 2Ch 7:20,21; La 2:15,16; Mic 6:16 shall be. De 28:59; Ps 22:7; 44:14; Isa 37:22; Mt 27:39; Mr 15:29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-17","title":"Jeremiah 18:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>scatter. 13:24; De 28:25,64; Job 27:21; Ps 48:7; Ho 13:15 shew. 2:27; 32:33; De 31:17; Jud 10:13,14 the day. 46:21; De 32:35; Pr 7:25,26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-18","title":"Jeremiah 18:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>Come. 11; 11:19; Ps 21:11; Isa 32:7; Mic 2:1-3 for the. 13:13,14; 14:14-16; 29:25-29; Le 10:11; 1Ki 22:24; Mal 2:7 Lu 11:45; Joh 7:47-49; 9:40 counsel. 2Sa 15:31; 17:14; Job 5:13 Come and let us smite. 26:11; Ps 52:2; 57:4; 64:3; Pr 18:21 with. or, for. and let us not. 5:12,13; 43:2; 44:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-19","title":"Jeremiah 18:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>Give. 20:12; Ps 55:16,17; 64:1-4; 56:1-3; 109:4,28; Mic 7:8; Lu 6:11,12 hearken. 2Ki 19:16; Ne 4:4,5; 6:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-20","title":"Jeremiah 18:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>evil. 1Sa 24:17-19; Ps 35:12; 38:20; 109:4,5; Pr 17:13; Joh 10:32; 15:25 digged. 22; Job 6:27; Ps 7:15; 35:7; 57:6; 119:95; Pr 26:27; Ec 10:8 Remember. 7:16; 11:14; 14:7-11,20-22; 15:1; Ge 18:22-32; Ps 106:23 Eze 22:30,31; Zec 3:1,2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-21","title":"Jeremiah 18:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>deliver. 11:20-23; 12:3; 20:1-6,11,12; Ps 109:9-20; 2Ti 4:14 pour out their blood. Heb. pour them out. let their wives. 15:2,3,8; 16:3,4; Ex 22:24; De 32:25; La 5:3 let their young. 9:21; 11:22; 2Ch 36:17; Am 4:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-22","title":"Jeremiah 18:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>a cry. 4:19,20,31; 6:26; 9:20,21; 25:34-36; 47:2,3; 48:3-5; Isa 10:30 Isa 22:1-4; Zep 1:10,11,16 for. 20 and hid. 20:10; Ps 38:12; 56:5-7; 64:4,5; 140:5; Mt 22:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-18-23","title":"Jeremiah 18:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>thou. 18; 11:18-20; 15:15; Ps 37:32,33 to slay me. Heb. for death. forgive. Ne 4:4,5; Ps 35:4; 59:5; 69:22-28; 109:14,15; Isa 2:9 in the. 8:12; 11:23; Isa 10:3; Lu 21:22; Ro 2:5</p>"}]}